The project tier wins over the core default: `core.auto_migrate: false` in the vault's
`config.yaml` turns the playbook-render gate back into the STOP notice for the user, and the
fixture playbook's preamble never appears.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
-- fixtures/home/Claude/probe/config.yaml --
core:
  auto_migrate: false
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-gated/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-gated
title: Gated
summary: Must not render while the vault is behind.
---

Preamble that a working gate suppresses.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-gated/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  only: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-gated/only/prompt.md --
---
name: only
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-gated
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
**STOP — tell the user:** this project is behind on booping migrations (recorded id -1, latest shipped [..]). Run `/playbook migrate` to bring the vault current, then retry.
-- stderr --
